{"id":"acef6b87926c62dd","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-proper-forcing-preservation.md","title":"Proper Forcing Preservation","display":"thm-proper-forcing-preservation — Proper Forcing Preservation","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-proper-forcing-preservation","aliases":["58-thm-proper-forcing-preservation","Proper Forcing Preservation","Stationary Set Preservation"],"display":"thm-proper-forcing-preservation — Proper Forcing Preservation","depends_on":["[[58-df-zfc-proper-poset]]","[[../batch06/58-df-ctm.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-name.md]]","[[58-df-satisfaction]]","[[58-df-structure]]","[[../batch03/58-df-assignment.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-proper-forcing-preservation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-proper-forcing-preservation</span><span>Proper Forcing Preservation</span><span>Stationary Set Preservation</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-proper-forcing-preservation — Proper Forcing Preservation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"bc6a9777ab02e72a\" href=\"?note=bc6a9777ab02e72a\" title=\"58-df-zfc-proper-poset\">58-df-zfc-proper-poset</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"66d43bb76d055059\" href=\"?note=66d43bb76d055059\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-ctm.md\">../batch06/58-df-ctm.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"46b2495f214783c3\" href=\"?note=46b2495f214783c3\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md\">../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ec28b62254928d73\" href=\"?note=ec28b62254928d73\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-name.md\">../batch07/58-df-name.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"58-df-satisfaction\">58-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"58-df-structure\">58-df-structure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-assignment.md\">../batch03/58-df-assignment.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,P,R,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}},\\varphi_{\\omega_1},\\check{\\omega_1^M}\\in V\">\\(M,P,R,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}},\\varphi_{\\omega_1},\\check{\\omega_1^M}\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\">\\(\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\\)</span> is the imported countable-transitive-model predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_{\\in}\">\\(\\mathcal L_{\\in}\\)</span> is the membership language, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}}(v_0,v_1)\">\\(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}}(v_0,v_1)\\)</span> is the formula code obtained by expanding the imported two-place proper-poset predicate in that language</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_{\\omega_1}(v_0)\">\\(\\varphi_{\\omega_1}(v_0)\\)</span> is the membership-language formula code saying that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_0\">\\(v_0\\)</span> is the least uncountable ordinal</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I^{\\mathcal M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}\">\\(I^{\\mathcal M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}\\)</span> are the imported satisfaction-data operations</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProperInModel}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ProperInModel}_S\\)</span> is the local satisfaction-based predicate defined below</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Name}\">\\(\\mathrm{Name}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\subseteq V^6\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\subseteq V^6\\)</span> are the imported name and fully parameterized forcing predicates</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}proper\\text{-}in\\text{-}model}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{ProperInModel}_S(M,P,R,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}})\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}}\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_{\\in})\n\\land\\exists\\mathcal M,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)=M\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal L_{\\in},\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{7em}{}\\land\\dot\\in\\,\\in\\mathcal L_{\\in}.\\mathrm{Rel}_2\n\\land I^{\\mathcal M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\n=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in M^2:x\\in y\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{7em}{}\\land s(v_0)=P\\land s(v_1)=R\n\\land\\operatorname{Sat}(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}},s)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}proper\\text{-}in\\text{-}model}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{ProperInModel}_S(M,P,R,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}})\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}}\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_{\\in})\n\\land\\exists\\mathcal M,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)=M\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal L_{\\in},\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{7em}{}\\land\\dot\\in\\,\\in\\mathcal L_{\\in}.\\mathrm{Rel}_2\n\\land I^{\\mathcal M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\n=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in M^2:x\\in y\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{7em}{}\\land s(v_0)=P\\land s(v_1)=R\n\\land\\operatorname{Sat}(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}},s)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}proper\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}preservation}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\n\\land P,R,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}},\\varphi_{\\omega_1},\\check{\\omega_1^M}\\in M\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{ProperInModel}_S(M,P,R,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}})\n\\land\\varphi_{\\omega_1}\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_{\\in})\n\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\check{\\omega_1^M},P)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\forall p\\in P\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\bigl(\nM,p,\\varphi_{\\omega_1},\n\\langle\\check{\\omega_1^M}\\rangle,P,R\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}proper\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}preservation}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\n\\land P,R,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}},\\varphi_{\\omega_1},\\check{\\omega_1^M}\\in M\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{ProperInModel}_S(M,P,R,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{proper}})\n\\land\\varphi_{\\omega_1}\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_{\\in})\n\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\check{\\omega_1^M},P)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\forall p\\in P\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\bigl(\nM,p,\\varphi_{\\omega_1},\n\\langle\\check{\\omega_1^M}\\rangle,P,R\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Shelah developed proper forcing theory; properness is the key iteration property behind PFA.</li>\n<li>The conclusion is a fully parameterized forcing assertion: every condition forces the check-name for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1^M\">\\(\\omega_1^M\\)</span> to remain the least uncountable ordinal.</li>\n<li>Internal properness is expressed through an actual formula code and satisfaction witness, rather than applying <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\\models\">\\(M\\models\\)</span> to the external semantic predicate <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProperPoset}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ProperPoset}_S\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>By the forcing theorem, every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span>-generic extension by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span> therefore satisfies <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1^{M[G]}=\\omega_1^M\">\\(\\omega_1^{M[G]}=\\omega_1^M\\)</span>; proper forcing also preserves stationary subsets of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1\">\\(\\omega_1\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Countable-support iterations of proper forcing preserve properness and stationarity in the standard theorem scheme.</li>\n<li>Applications: iteration, forcing axioms.</li>\n<li>Weaker than ccc: allows more forcings.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-zfc-proper-poset","status":"resolved","id":"bc6a9777ab02e72a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-proper-poset]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch06/58-df-ctm.md","status":"resolved","id":"66d43bb76d055059","anchor":"ref-2","target